# Milestone: M5
# Covers: at (cond) body — rising-edge fire; body runs once when condition
#         transitions false→true; does not re-fire if condition stays true.
#
# defer-to: M5-scratch-frame
#
# Reason:
#   invoke_condition_closure and run_closure_on_scratch_frame_with_result are
#   M5-stub functions (uwatcher_eval.c / uwatcher_install.c); both return
#   UVAL_NIL unless the test_watcher_condition_hook or test_install_cond_hook
#   is set.  End-to-end script-level condition evaluation and body dispatch
#   require the scratch-frame execution path to be wired (M5 proper).
#   Rising/falling edge logic is exercised by test_at_fire_paths.c T43 unit
#   tests using those hooks.
#
# Activate when scratch-frame execution is wired by replacing the source below.
#
# Urbiscript source (activate at M5 scratch-frame):
#   var x = 0;
#   var fired = 0;
#   at (x > 5) Realm.fired = Realm.fired + 1;
#   Realm.x = 10;
#   fired
#   --- expected output ---
#   [00000000] 0
#   [00000001] 0
#   [00000002] nil
#   [00000003] 10
#   [00000004] 1
